34
00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:21.000
about pursuing, you know, really short-term, massive businesses like this. A 2023 report from the commercial real estate data company CoStar says the United States has more than 50 square feet of retail space per person. A 2023 report from the commercial real estate data company CoStar says the United States has more than 50 square feet of retail space per person. That's much higher than countries like Australia, which have about 11 square feet. European countries have even less. And in Rachel's opinion, the success of Spirit is something that only happens because we
老实说，对于现在所有闲置的大型卖场，我认为最好的情况是把它们推倒，让它们回归土地，特别是当它们位于城镇边缘、没有车就很难到达的地方时。

35
00:18:21.000 --> 00:19:00.000
have a bunch of big companies that build big boxes and then leave them empty. Honestly, for all the huge big box stores that are now sitting vacant, I think the best case scenario is to knock them down, let them return to the earth, particularly if they're on the edge of town where it's hard to access without a car. I don't think that's a viable model to hope that we could transform all these stores into something new, especially when there's more and more becoming vacant every day. For his part, Mike Olson doesn't agree that there's some big overabundance of retail space.
就他而言，迈克·奥尔森不同意零售空间存在巨大过剩的说法。

