00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:36.000
In fact, he says right now, it's kind of a low point in the market for Spirit. We're in a completely different era. We're at a point where it's difficult to find spaces because there hasn't been much in the way of new construction for retail across the country. And what retail is out there happens to be mixed use, you know, retail on the main floor, apartments or office above. If Mike's right, Spirit still manages to find hundreds of empty storefronts every year. The days of Spirit's real estate team driving around and begging landlords for space, those are over.
如果迈克是对的，“万圣节幽灵”每年依然能找到数百个空置店面。“万圣节幽灵”的房地产团队开车到处求房东给个铺位的日子已经一去不复返了。

37
00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:56.000
Today, larger corporate landlords expect Spirit's calls every year. And those calls start as early as January. That's because Spirit is just a regular part of their business now. Look, we are no different than any other retailer out there right now, because they're doing the exact same thing.
如今，较大的企业房东每年都在期待“万圣节幽灵”的电话。而这些电话早在1月就开始打了。

38
00:19:56.000 --> 00:20:15.000
I guarantee you, it's just on a slower scale. Every retailer is a temporary tenant. It just depends on how long they're temporary. Sears was temporary for 130 years. Other tenants, well, they're temporary for two years. You know? But that's the reality of retail. Ultimately, Spirit isn't the reason
听着，我们现在和其他任何零售商没什么不同，因为他们在做完全相同的事情。

39
00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:38.000
for empty big box stores. There are bigger factors at play here. I don't think that there's something inherently wrong with Spirit. It's more like a symptom of a bigger problem. Most of our cities today, unfortunately, are really structured to invite those large scale developments. Our zoning codes, our rules around parking requirements,
我不认为“万圣节幽灵”本身有什么不对。它更像是一个更大问题的症状。

